    "definitive_conclusion": "The disappearance of H1 and H2 specificity signals in Stage B-8 was 100% caused by implementation/definition defects (loss of target centroid, orthogonalization against absolute origin vector, and zero-norm cancellation). When tested under the rigorous B-7 residual orthogonalization definition on the expanded B-8 dataset (Cell 2,1), ortho28+kasane11 on Class A achieves p=0.0175 vs rand (p=0.0051 vs other), and 6pole+HW-25 on Class B achieves p=0.0164 vs rand (p=0.0018 vs other), confirming that the two-scale lens hypothesis holds robustly across pair expansion."
